{{sbc|Active:}} '''Akshan''' throws a boomerang in the target direction that briefly grants {{tip|sight}} around its trajectory and deals {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit, {{tip|standard sight|revealing}} them for 1 second and extending its range each time it hits a target. If this hits an enemy {{tip|champion}}, '''Akshan''' gains {{sti|ms|{{as|20%|ms}}}} {{as|(+ 5% per 100 AP)}} {{as|'''bonus''' movement speed}} that decays over 1 second.
Once the boomerang has passed its original range and has not hit a target in the last 500 units of travelling, it homes back to '''Akshan''' and applies the same effects to enemies hit.
''Avengerang'' deals reduced damage against non-champions.
''Enemies can be hit only once per pass.''
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|45 to 165}} {{as|(+ 70% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Total Physical Damage|{{ap|45*2 to 165*2}} {{as|(+ {{ap|70*2}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Non-Champion Damage|{{ap|40 to 80}}%}}
{{tt|{{ap|9 to 5}}|Starts after the boomerang returns}}
{{ap|60 to 80}}
Mana
Physical
* {{tip|Spell shield}} will only block a single hit. They do not prevent the initial throw from extending its range.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
* This ability's damage is calculated based on the caster's current stats and changes dynamically.
<!-- Blurb -->

The icon of this ability reflects the next weapon that is in reserve.
{{sbc|Active:}} '''Aphelios''' receives a text prompt of the weapon '''Alune''' will create next.
* This ability also includes the icon of the {{as|off-hand}}.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Ashe''' shoots a volley of arrows in a cone in the target direction, each dealing {{as|physical damage}} to the first enemy hit, and applying ''{{ai|Frost Shot 2|Ashe|Critical Slow}}'' to enemy {{tip|champions}} hit.
Enemies can intercept multiple arrows but do not take damage from any beyond the first.
{{st|Arrows|{{ap|7 to 11}}}}
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|60 to 200}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{ap|18 to 4}}
{{ap|75 to 55}}
Mana
Physical
* The missiles are spawned in a straight horizontal line 75 units in front of '''Ashe''', with a total width of 75/100/100/123/123 units.
** Between each missile spawn location is a distance of {{fd|12.5}} units, except for the two outermost ones at the last two ranks (which are {{fd|11.5}} units from the closest other one), and the two centermost missiles at ranks 2 and 4 (which have 20 units between them and 15 units to the next missile, respectively).
** This inconsistent behaviour of spawn locations means the angle between each missile can vary off of {{fd|4.625}}{{degrees}} slighty.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
<!--Blurb-->

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Azir''' orders all {{as|Sand Soldiers|buzzword2}} to dash toward the target location, dealing {{as|magic damage}} to all enemies they pass through as well as those in front of them upon arrival, and {{tip|slow|slowing}} them by 25% for 1 second.
Enemies hit by subsequent soldiers take no additional damage or {{tip|slow}}.
''A summoned {{as|Sand Soldier|buzzword2}} is required to cast this ability.''
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|60 to 140}} {{as|(+ {{ap|35 to 55}}% AP)}}}}
{{ap|14 to 6}}
{{ap|70 to 110}}
mana
Magic
* {{as|Sand Soldiers|buzzword2}} dash about 50 units further away from Azir than the target location, making them stab targets slightly further away.
* {{as|Sand Soldiers|buzzword2}} will stop their movement upon colliding with {{ai|Wind Wall|Yasuo}} or {{ai|Rebuttal|Mel}}, but not {{ai|Unbreakable|Braum}}.
* {{as|Sand Soldiers|buzzword2}} will automatically turn to face nearby enemy champions after the dash.
** This happens even if they're in {{tip|stealth}}.{{bug}}
* If there are multiple active {{as|Sand Soldiers|buzzword2}}, rather than all soldiers arriving at the target location they make a formation around it instead.
** If the number of soldiers is 2, then neither will arrive at the location.
** If the number of soldiers is greater than 2, then 1 soldier will arrive at the location and the rest will arrive around it.
** This can produce unexpected results as soldiers arrive at different distances and locations and the determination of the placement is undocumented.
*** This has gameplay implications for casting at max range.{{bug}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Azir''' grants himself a {{tip|shield}} for {{fd|1.5}} seconds and {{tip|dashes}} to the {{as|Sand Soldier|buzzword2}} closest to the cursor, dealing {{as|magic damage}} to enemies within his path.
If '''Azir''' dashes into an enemy {{tip|champion}}, he stops and gains a charge of ''{{ai|Arise!|Azir}}''.
''A summoned {{as|Sand Soldier|buzzword2}} is required to cast this ability. '''Azir''' can cast any of his [[champion ability|abilities]] during the dash.''
{{st|Shield Strength|{{ap|70 to 230}} {{as|(+ 60% AP)}}}}
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|70 to 230}} {{as|(+ 60% AP)}}}}
{{ap|22 to 16}}
60
mana
Magic
* '''Azir''' will track the {{as|Sand Soldier|buzzword2}} if they change locations, such as by {{ai|Conquering Sands|Azir}}.
* Movement and attack commands will be canceled upon cast and cannot be issued again until '''Azir''' arrives at his final location.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Caitlyn''' fires a piercing shot in the target direction that deals {{as|physical damage}} to the first enemy it passes through, after which it expands in width but deals only 60% damage to enemies it hits thereafter.
Enemies {{tip|true sight|revealed}} by ''{{ai|Yordle Snap Trap|Caitlyn}}'' always take {{ccs|full damage|physical}} from ''Piltover Peacemaker''.
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|50 to 210}} {{as|(+ {{ap|125 to 205}}% AD)}}|Reduced Damage|{{ap|50*0.6 to 210*0.6}} {{as|(+ {{ap|125*0.6 to 205*0.6}}% AD)}}}}
{{ap|10 to 6}}
{{ap|55 to 75}}
mana
Physical
* Upon ''Piltover Peacemaker'' dealing damage to an enemy, '''Caitlyn's''' [[attack timer]] is forcibly {{tip|basic attack reset|reset}}.{{bug}}
* Enemies hit while protected by a {{tip|spell shield}} will still be considered a target for calculating damage for subsequent hits.
{{Effect at cast time start}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Caitlyn''' sets a visible trap at the target location that is {{tip|untargetable}} and arms after 1 second, lasting for a duration. The trap grants {{tip|sight}} of the area for 1 second after being placed.
'''Caitlyn''' periodically [[ammunition|stocks]] a ''Yordle Snap Trap'' charge, up to a maximum amount. Deploying traps beyond the maximum destroys the oldest one.
The next enemy champion that springs the trap is {{tip|root|rooted}} for {{fd|1.5}} seconds and {{tip|true sight|revealed}} for 3 seconds, as well as takes additional damage from the ''{{ai|Headshot|Caitlyn}}'' granted by this ability. Trapped targets become immune to further ''Yordle Snap Traps'' for 3 seconds, preventing them from springing subsequent traps for the duration.
{{st|Trap Duration|{{ap|30 to 50}} seconds}}
{{st|Maximum Number of Traps|{{ap|3|3|4|4|5}}}}
{{st|{{ai|Headshot|Caitlyn}} Damage Increase|{{ap|35 to 215}} {{as|(+ 30% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{fd|0.5}}
20
Mana + 1 Charge
* Multiple armed traps on the same location will spring all at once if an enemy steps on one of them.

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Caitlyn''' fires a net in the target direction and {{tip|dash|recoils}} 390 units in the opposite direction. The net deals {{as|magic damage}} to the first enemy hit and {{tip|slow|slows}} them by 50% for 1 second.
'''''Caitlyn''' will not recoil after the cast time if she was {{tip|immobilize|immobilized}} or {{tip|ground|grounded}} during it. She can cast any of her [[champion ability|abilities]] during the recoil dash.''
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|80 to 280}} {{as|(+ 80% AP)}}}}
{{ap|16 to 8}}
75
mana
Magic
{{Effect at cast time end}}
* The recoil can be used to pass through terrain.
* If '''Caitlyn''' buffers {{ai|Piltover Peacemaker|Caitlyn}} during ''90 Caliber Net's'' cast time, {{ai|Piltover Peacemaker|Caitlyn}} will start after the cast time.
** If '''Caitlyn''' buffers an ability or [[basic attack]] during this ability's cast time, the buffered ability or basic attack will instead start after the dash ends.
** Other abilities can be cast while {{tip|dash|dashing}} if they are input after the cast time.
* ''90 Caliber Net's'' missile will fail to fire if '''Caitlyn''' is {{tip|suppression|suppressed}} during the cast time.{{bug|2}}
}}

{{sbc|Innate:}} '''Corki's''' {{tip|basic attacks}} deal {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' true damage}}}} equal to {{as|20% AD}}. This damage is affected by {{tip|critical strike}} modifiers. Additionally, spell blade effects provide extra triggers.
Physical True
* The mixed damage is dealt in two simultaneous instances of damage, but will pretend to be a single instance for most effects (such as {{ris|Conqueror}} stacks).
** The {{as|true damage}} is dealt in an instance before the {{as|physical damage}}.
** Both instances deal {{tip|basic damage}} and thus natively apply {{as|{{sti|life steal}}}}.
** The attack applies {{tip|on-hit}} effects only once, right at the start.
** Even if the target dies from the {{as|true damage}}, the {{as|physical damage}} will still be applied to it.
*** If the target dies from {{tip|on-hit}} damage, the true damage portion will be skipped and only the physical damage applied.{{bug}}
** {{iis|Runaan's Hurricane}} {{nie|Wind's Fury}} and {{tip|Spellblade}} effects have both been special cased to benefit from ''Hextech Munitions'', causing them to deal {{as|'''bonus''' true damage}} equal to 20% of the {{tt|pre-mitigation damage|Damage calculated before modifiers}} dealt.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Corki''' launches a bomb at the target location that briefly grants {{tip|sight}} of its {{tt|surroundings|Cannot grant sight through terrain and can only grant sight into brush when the missile flies through that brush}} as it travels and explodes upon impact, dealing {{as|magic damage}} to enemies hit.
The bomb also grants {{tip|sight}} of the impact area for 6 seconds and {{tip|standard sight|reveals}} enemy {{tip|champions}} hit for the same duration.
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|60 to 240}} {{as|(+ 125% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ 100% AP)}}}}
{{ap|9 to 7}}
{{ap|60 to 80}}
mana
Magic
* The missile has a minimum travel time of {{fd|0.227}} seconds.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Corki''' {{tip|dashes}} to the target location and drops bombs that leave up to 3 blazing patches along his path, depending on the distance traveled. Each patch lasts {{fd|2.5}} seconds.
Enemies within the patches are dealt {{as|magic damage}} every {{fd|0.5}} seconds, lingering for 1 second.
''{{ai|Gatling Gun|Corki}} can be cast during the dash.''
{{st|Magic Damage Per Tick|{{ap|30 to 90}} {{as|(+ 40% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ 30% AP)}}|Total Magic Damage|{{ap|30*5 to 90*5}} {{as|(+ {{ap|40*5}}% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ {{ap|30*5}}% AP)}}}}
{{ap|20 to 12}}
{{ap|80 to 100}}
mana
Magic
* No additional information.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Corki''' sprays bullets in a cone toward his facing direction for 4 seconds, dealing {{as|physical damage}} every {{fd|0.25}} seconds to all enemies hit and applying a {{tip|stack}} to them at the same tick rate for 2 seconds, refreshing with subsequent hits and stacking up to 4 times. Each stack reduces the target's {{sti|lethality|{{as|armor}}}} and {{sti|magic penetration|{{as|magic resistance}}}}.
{{st|Physical Damage Per Tick|{{ap|80/16 to 280/16}} {{as|(+ {{ap|240/16}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}|Total Physical Damage|{{ap|80 to 280}} {{as|(+ 240% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Resistances Reduction Per Stack|{{ap|3 to 5}}|Total Resistances Reduction|{{ap|3*4 to 5*4}}}}
12
{{ap|50 to 70}}
mana
physical
* The maximum resistances reduction is applied after 4 ticks (1 second).
* The direction of the gun firing changes depending on where '''Corki''' is facing.
** '''Corki''' will turn to face in the direction of the cursor upon casting ''Gatling Gun''. He will also instantly turn when issuing an Attack order on enemies while ''Gatling Gun'' is active.
** Issuing an Attack Move order at a location will not cause '''Corki''' to instantly turn.{{bug|2}}
* ''Gatling Gun's'' area of effect can hit close by enemies next to and behind him, due to registering {{tip|er|enemies' edge}}.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Draven''' enters an adrenaline rush, gaining {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' attack speed}}}} for 3 seconds as well as decaying {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' movement speed}}}} and {{tip|ghosting}} for {{fd|1.5}} seconds.
Catching a ''{{ai|Spinning Axe|Draven}}'' resets ''Blood Rush's'' {{sti|cooldown}}.
{{st|Bonus Attack Speed|{{ap|20 to 40}}%}}
{{st|Bonus Movement Speed|{{ap|50 to 70}}%}}
12
{{ap|40 to 20}}
Mana
* Activating ''Blood Rush'' while the effect is already active will refresh the duration.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Draven''' throws a fan of axes in a line in the target direction, dealing {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit, {{tip|airborne|knocking them aside}}, though not through terrain, and {{tip|slow|slowing}} them for 2 seconds.
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|75 to 215}} {{as|(+ 50% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}{{st|Slow|{{ap|20 to 40}}%}}
{{ap|16 to 12}}
70
Mana
Physical
{{Effect at cast time end}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Draven''' hurls two massive axes in the target direction that briefly grant {{tip|sight}} of their surroundings and deal {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit. Enemy {{tip|champions}} that are damaged to or while below a {{sti|{{as|health}}}} threshold equal to the number of ''{{ai|League of Draven|Draven|Adoration}}'' stacks are {{tip|execute|executed}}.
''Whirling Death'' can be recast after 1 second while the axes are traveling, and does so automatically after the axes hit an enemy {{tip|champion}} or the edge of the [[Map (League of Legends)|map]].
{{sbc|Recast:}} '''Draven''' forces the axes to reverse direction, slowly coming to a stop before homing back to him, dealing the same damage to enemies hit.
''Whirling Death'' deals {{pp|key=%|type=enemies hit|100*0.95^(x-1);50|x-1 for 15|formula=(100%-5%)^(1 per enemy hit). ''This is capped at 50% damage.''}} damage, resetting upon reversing direction.
''Enemies can be hit only once per pass.''
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|200 to 400}} {{as|(+ {{ap|110 to 150}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}|Total Physical Damage|{{ap|200*2 to 400*2}} {{as|(+ {{ap|110*2 to 150*2}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Minimum Physical Damage|{{ap|200*0.5 to 400*0.5}} {{as|(+ {{ap|110*0.5 to 150*0.5}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}|Minimum Total Damage|{{ap|200*0.5*2 to 400*0.5*2}} {{as|(+ {{ap|110*0.5*2 to 150*0.5*2}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{ap|100 to 80}}
100
mana
Physical
* ''Whirling Death's'' projectile has an [[File:Whirling Death Minimap.png|40px|link=]] icon on the mini-map while it is in flight. It can be seen by only '''Draven''' and his allies.
* {{tip|Spell shield}} will block one instance of damage.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
}}

{{sbc|Innate:}} '''Ezreal''' generates a {{tip|stack}} of ''Rising Spell Force'' for each enemy hit by his {{tip|abilities}}, lasting for 6 seconds, refreshing on subsequent hits, and stacking up to 5 times.
{{sbc|Rising Spell Force:}} For each stack, '''Ezreal''' gains {{sti|as|{{as|10% '''bonus''' attack speed}}}}, up to a maximum of {{as|50%|attack speed}}.
* ''Rising Spell Force'' will stack even if the abilities hit were blocked by {{tip|spell shield|spell shields}}.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Ezreal''' fires a bolt of energy in the target direction that deals {{as|physical damage}} to the first enemy hit, applying {{tip|on-hit}} effects and triggering {{tip|on-attack}} effects.
If ''Mystic Shot'' successfully hits an enemy, the {{sti|'''current''' cooldowns}} of '''Ezreal's''' abilities, including ''Mystic Shot's'', are reduced by {{fd|1.5}} seconds.
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|20 to 120}} {{as|(+ 130% AD)}} {{as|(+ 40% AP)}}}}
{{ap|5.5 to 4.5}}
{{ap|28 to 40}}
Mana
Physical
* ''Mystic Shot'' deals {{tip|basic damage}}, but also triggers spell effects by also being tagged as {{tip|spell damage}}.
* ''Mystic Shot'' benefits from {{as|{{sti|life steal}}}}, {{tip|omnivamp}}, and {{tip|physical vamp}}, but not {{tip|spell vamp}}.
* Even if the ability is blocked by {{tip|spell shield}} it will still trigger the cooldown reduction.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
* ''Mystic Shot'' will be buffered and cast when the cooldown ends if the player attempts to cast it within {{fd|0.05}} seconds of the cooldown ending.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Ezreal''' {{tip|blinks}} from his current location to up to 475 units towards the target location, then fires a homing bolt towards the nearest enemy that deals {{as|magic damage}} and {{tip|standard sight|reveals}} them for 1 second.
''Arcane Shift'' prioritizes firing at the nearest enemy marked by ''{{ai|Essence Flux|Ezreal}}''.
''The target does not have to be {{tip|sight|visible}} to be hit by this ability.''
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|80 to 280}} {{as|(+ 60% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ 75% AP)}}}}
{{ap|26 to 14}}
70
Mana
Magic
* If '''Ezreal''' is moved during the cast time, his range to blink will update accordingly. This does not exceed the maximum target range.
* The target is revealed as soon as '''Ezreal''' fires the missile at them.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Ezreal''' fires a powerful arc of energy in the target direction that briefly grants {{tip|sight}} of its surroundings and deals {{as|magic damage}} to enemies hit.
{{tip|Minion|Minions}} and non-epic {{tip|monster|monsters}} take modified damage.
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|350 to 750}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ 110% AP)}}}}
{{st|Modified Damage|{{ap|150 to 300}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ 110% AP)}}}}
{{ap|120 to 90}}
100
Mana
Magic
* ''Trueshot Barrage's'' projectile has an [[File:Trueshot Barrage Minimap.png|40px|link=]] icon on the mini-map while it is in flight. It can be seen by only '''Ezreal''' and his allies.
{{Effect at cast time start}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Graves''' fires a round in the target direction that deals {{as|physical damage}} to enemies it passes through and leaves behind a powder trail.
After 2 seconds, or {{rutngt|0.2}} upon colliding with terrain, the round detonates to deal {{as|physical damage}} to enemies within a wide perpendicular area and in a reverse wave along the powder trail.
''Enemies can only be hit once per pass.''
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|50 to 150}} {{as|(+ 65% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|80 to 260}} {{as|(+ {{ap|55 to 115}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}|Total Physical Damage|{{ap|50+80 to 150+260}} {{as|(+ {{ap|65+55 to 65+115}}% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{ap|13 to 6}}
80
Mana
Physical
* {{tip|Spell shield|Spell shields}} can only block one instance of the ability's damage.
* {{ai|Wind Wall|Yasuo}} will destroy the projectile entirely and mitigate all effects, including the trail on the ground.
* {{ai|Unbreakable|Braum}} is considered to be terrain for the purposes of the projectile, triggering its second effect.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Graves''' fires a smoke canister at the target location that upon impact deals {{as|magic damage}} to enemies within the area and {{tip|slow|slows}} them by 50% for {{fd|0.5}} seconds.
The canister creates a cloud of smoke for 4 seconds that applies {{tip|nearsight}} of outside the area to all enemies within every {{fd|0.25}} seconds, reducing their {{tip|sight}} radius relative to the center.
{{st|Magic Damage|{{ap|60 to 260}} {{as|(+ 60% AP)}}}}
{{ap|26 to 18}}
{{ap|70 to 90}}
Mana
Magic
* ''Smoke Screen'' will {{tip|nearsight}} {{tip|untargetable}} units.
* {{tip|Spell shield|Spell shields}} will block the instance of damage and {{tip|slow}}, but will not mitigate the persistent area of effect.
* {{tip|cc-immune|Crowd control immunity}} and {{tip|cleanse|cleanses}} have no effect on the user's {{tip|sight}} radius reduction despite the {{tip|nearsight}} being resisted / removed. Loss of allied vision will still be affected.{{bug|2}}
** Removing or resisting the nearsight will prevent it from being reapplied while staying inside the area (leaving and coming back inside will not).
* The nearsight debuff applies to non-champions but it does not inherently stop them from performing actions that require {{tip|sight}}, such as [[basic attack]]ing.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Graves''' {{tip|dashes}} to the target location, reloading one {{as|shell|buzzword3}} while generating a {{tip|stack}} of ''True Grit'' for 4 seconds, stacking up to 8 times. Dashing towards an enemy {{tip|champion}} generates 2 stacks of ''True Grit''.
''Quickdraw's'' {{sti|'''current''' cooldown}} is reduced by {{fd|0.5}} seconds for every {{as|pellet|buzzword2}} impacting an enemy.
{{sbc|True Grit:}} For each stack, '''Graves''' gains {{sti|armor|{{as|'''bonus''' armor}}}}, and {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' magic resistance}}}} equal to 50% of that amount. Subsequent casts of ''Quickdraw'' and damage versus non-{{tip|minions}} will refresh the duration of ''True Grit''.
''Quickdraw {{tip|basic attack reset|resets}} '''Graves'''' basic attack timer.''
{{st|Bonus Armor|{{ap|7 to 19}}|Maximum Bonus Armor|{{ap|7*8 to 19*8}}}}
{{st|Bonus Magic Resistance|{{ap|7*0.5 to 19*0.5}}|Maximum Bonus MR|{{ap|7*0.5*8 to 19*0.5*8}}}}
{{ap|16 to 12}}
40
Mana
* If '''Graves''' dashes while reloading, he can cast any of his {{tip|abilities}} during the dash.{{bug|1}}
* '''Graves''' gains the one additional stack of ''True Grit'' from ''Quickdraw'' if at any point during the dash a {{tip|sight|visible}} enemy champion is in front of ''Graves'' within {{tip|er|icononly = true}} 1300 distance.
** Enemy champions have to be targetable to grant the additional stack.
** The additional stack of ''True Grit'' is gained when dashing towards {{tip|clone|clones}} just like actual champions.
** This check never happens if '''Graves''' dashes 0 distance (impossible outside of bugs), and will not always repeat a final time at the very end of the dash. Otherwise, it occurs continously while '''Graves''' is dashing.
** This works for a 180 degree sector from Graves to the Champion, as such dashing parallel to the champ will also give a bonus stack.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Graves''' fires an explosive shell in the target direction that deals {{as|physical damage}} to enemies hit and causes him to {{tip|dash|recoil}} 400 units in the opposite direction.
Upon hitting an enemy {{tip|champion}} or reaching the end of its range, the shell explodes in a cone to deal reduced damage to additional enemies.
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|275 to 575}} {{as|(+ 150% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Reduced Damage|{{ap|200 to 440}} {{as|(+ 120% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{ap|100 to 60}}
100
Mana
Physical
* Applies {{tip|spell damage}} to the target hit by the shell (including to non-champions struck before exploding{{bug}}) and {{tip|area damage}} to targets within the explosion cone.
* The projectile will still explode early if the champion hit by the shell is protected by a {{tip|spell shield}}.
* The explosion cone is anchored on the location of the shell missile when it collided with a champion, or otherwise its maximum cast range.
* The cone damage is always located 150 units behind, based off its direction
* ''Collateral Damage'' is not disabled while {{tip|ground|grounded}} or {{tip|root|rooted}}, but '''Graves''' will not dash after the cast time while affected by them.
* '''Graves''' will not {{tip|dash}} after the cast time if he is {{tip|airborne}}.
{{Effect at cast time end}}
}}

{{sbc|Innate:}} Whenever '''Jayce''' switches between either {{sbc|{{ai|Transform Mercury Hammer|Jayce|Hammer Stance}}}} or {{sbc|{{ai|Transform Mercury Cannon|Jayce|Cannon Stance}}}}, he gains {{tip|ghosting}} and {{sti|ms|{{as|30 '''bonus''' movement speed}}}} for {{fd|0.75}} seconds.
* No additional details.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Jayce''' {{tip|dash|leaps}} to the target enemy's location over {{fd|0.5}} seconds. Upon arrival, he smashes his hammer to the ground to deal {{as|physical damage}} to all enemies within an area and {{tip|slow}} them for 2 seconds.
''To the Skies!'' deals {{as|10 '''bonus''' physical damage}} to {{tip|monsters}}.
''{{ai|Lightning Field|Jayce}} can be cast during the dash.''
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|60 to 310 6}} {{as|(+ 135% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Slow|{{ap|35 to 60 6}}%}}
{{ap|16 to 6 6}}
40
Mana
physical
* ''To The Skies!'' will always direct '''Jayce''' linearly to his target's location.

{{sbc|Passive:}} '''Jayce's''' {{tip|basic attacks}} restore {{sti|{{as|mana}}}} {{tip|on-hit}}.
{{sbc|Active:}} '''Jayce''' surrounds himself with an electric field for 4 seconds that deals {{as|magic damage}} every second to nearby enemies.
{{st|Mana Restored|{{as|{{ap|15 to 25 6}}|Mana}}}}
{{st|Magic Damage Per Tick|{{ap|35 to 110 6}} {{as|(+ 25% AP)}}|Total Magic Damage|{{ap|35*4 to 110*4 6}} {{as|(+ 100% AP)}}}}
10
40
Mana
magic
* The {{as|{{sti|mana}}}} restore triggers on {{tip|structures}}.
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Jayce''' {{tip|root|roots}} the target enemy over the cast time, then swings his hammer at them to deal {{as|magic damage}}, capped against {{tip|monsters}}, and {{tip|airborne|knock them back}} 600 units.
'''''Jayce''' is unable to cast {{ai|To the Skies!|Jayce}} or {{ai|Shock Blast|Jayce}} for {{fd|0.4}} seconds after Thundering Blow's cast time.''
{{st|Magic Damage|{{as|{{ap|8 to 22 6}}% of target's '''maximum''' health}} {{as|(+ 100% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
{{st|Capped Monster Damage|{{ap|200 to 700 6}}}}
{{ap|20 to 10 6}}
55
Mana
magic
{{Unit-targeted cancel conditions}}
}}

{{sbc|Active:}} '''Jhin''' throws a grenade at the target enemy that deals {{as|physical damage}} and can bounce to up to three additional nearby enemies, prioritizing the closest enemy that has not been hit.
The grenade's damage is increased by 35% any time an enemy dies by any means after being hit by the grenade before it strikes its next target.
{{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|44 to 144}} {{as|(+ {{ap|44 to 74}}% AD)}} {{as|(+ 60% AP)}}}}
{{st|Bonus Damage per Target Death|{{ap|(44 to 144)*0.35}} {{as|(+ {{ap|(44 to 74)*0.35}}% AD)}} {{as|(+ {{ap|60*0.35}}% AP)}}}}
{{st|Maximum Final Bounce Physical Damage|{{ap|(44 to 144)*(1+0.35*3)}} {{as|(+ {{ap|(44 to 74)*(1+0.35*3)}}% AD)}} {{as|(+ {{ap|60*(1+0.35*3)}}% AP)}}}}
{{ap|7 to 5}}
{{ap|40 to 60}}
Mana
Physical
* {{tip|Spell shield}} will not prevent the canister from bouncing.
